Corpus tests: searched raw/daughters/celtic-stageC/units.jsonl for heart/mind, leaves/flowers, and joyful water. Found 43 heart/mind proximity hits, 20 leaves/flowers proximity hits, and one joyful-water hit (these are string-search counts, not independent formula attestations). Searched all Latin LASLA conllup files: flowers/leaves cooccur at LucrDRN5 5.1400 only at the citation-unit granularity used; no cor/mens pair at that granularity. Searched both available Atharvaveda DCS traditions: 11 Saunaka and 13 Paippalada sentence cooccurrences of manas with hrd/hrdaya. Read relevant lexical entries in data/lexicon/lexicon.jsonl. All raw access used python3 -I text reads; no raw code executed/imported.
Final adjudication: BS-83dca rejected as shared psychological vocabulary without shared construction: Irish menman is genitive dependent on toilg, coordinated with aicnid; cridi is governed by i. Vedic hrda/manasa are coordinated instrumentals in a desire for Indra/cattle. Wider Irish coordination includes religious material and cannot repair this slab-anchor mismatch. BS-b50c6/BS-ce780 rejected: Irish simultaneous leaf/flower growth (with fruit in the latter) versus Latin garland materials in festive dancing is an ordinary botanical pairing; duille/folium etymology is uncertain, with alternative initial aspirates in the local lexicon. BS-67f27 rejected: watery gladness lacks a distinctive shared cognate collocation. BS-6df9f cosmic merism lacks corresponding wording in its Greek anchor. BS-0ce23 cattle/animals rejected for generic enumeration and different mil/mela etymology. Other bundles lack defensible inherited phraseology.
